<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Hamburg Trip</name><Style id="doener"><IconStyle><color>ff2e57e4</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="skate"><IconStyle><color>ffab862e</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="history"><IconStyle><color>ff9b4e6b</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="games"><IconStyle><color>ff4a9d2a</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="music"><IconStyle><color>ff17a0d4</color><scale>1.1</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Folder><name>🥙 Döner</name><Placemark><name>Lokmam Köz (Schanze)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Susannenstraße 16. Blogger&#x27;s #2: big portions, intense flavours, Falstaff gold medal; 4.8★ with 8,400+ reviews per the same source.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Closest big-name pick to the Schanze skatepark (Rote Flora).]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.96389,53.56236,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kardelen (Neustadt)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Steinwegpassage 6, central near the Michel. Cheap (1–10 €), fast service, queue is normal; free flatbread at the counter per the source.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Best walkable option between Landungsbrücken and the city centre.]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.98238,53.55086,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Köz Antep (St. Pauli)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Clemens-Schultz-Straße 26, a few minutes from the Reeperbahn. Owner makes the döner himself, without the usual German seasoning — authentic Turkish style; the lahmacun is praised too. Not everyone&#x27;s taste.]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.96404,53.55214,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kebab House Kurtulan (Bahrenfeld)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Leverkusenstraße 2. Blogger&#x27;s #1 &#x27;best döner in Hamburg&#x27;: fresh spit daily, house-made avocado sauce, queue out the door at lunch. TAKEAWAY ONLY.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Out in Bahrenfeld — plan a short ride (also near Altona/Övelgönne side of the ferry route).]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.92656,53.56439,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Batman (Steindamm)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Steindamm 58, St. Georg near the main station. Named after the Turkish city, not the superhero. House-made sauces, fresh flatbread daily.]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.01454,53.55425,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Döner Queen (Winterhude)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Jarrestraße 57. Huge portions, juicy meat, vegan seitan option, free tea after the meal.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Near the Barmbek gaming spots (Cosmos Arcade / Retro Spiele Club).]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.02657,53.5854,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Traum Döner (Hammerbrook)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Spaldingstraße 55. Rated 4.9★ (479 reviews) and #1 on the hamburglist.com ranking — a second opinion to the blog list.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Close to I-Punkt Skateland (Hammerbrook).]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.01364,53.54861,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Honest Kebab (Ballindamm)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Ballindamm 40 (Europa Passage). Premium 100 % grass-fed beef, no additives; owned by YouTuber &#x27;Holle 21614&#x27;. Pricier.]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.99632,53.55147,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Sphinx Döner (Landwehr)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Landwehr 39, Eilbek/Hohenfelde. Old-school döner-shack feel, cheap, outdoor seating.]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.03737,53.5615,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Falafelstern (Schanze)</name><styleUrl>#doener</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Schanzenstraße 111. Best vegan döner/falafel per the source — handy if Irena joins another time.]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.96532,53.56441,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>🛹 Skate</name><Placemark><name>Kelle Skatepark (Loogeplatz)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Eppendorf, right next to U-Bahn Kellinghusenstraße. 870 m², room for ~60 skaters; concrete.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Easy U-Bahn trip (U1/U3).<br><a href="https://www.hamburg.de/freizeit/aktivitaeten/skateparks-hamburg-artikel-309220">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.99086,53.58839,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Skatepark an der Roten Flora (Schanze)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Behind the Rote Flora: cradle, micro ramp, rainbow coping, rollins. Concrete. Small but characterful, right in the Schanze.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Pair with Lokmam Köz / Falafelstern.<br><a href="https://www.hamburg.de/freizeit/aktivitaeten/skateparks-hamburg-artikel-309220">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.96129,53.56213,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>I-Punkt Skateland (Hammerbrook)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[1,500 m² covered hall + 1,800 m² outdoor area: street course, bowl, mini ramp, halfpipe. Weather-proof option.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Hours per hamburg.de: Mon/Tue/Thu 15–20, Wed/Fri 15–24, Sat/Sun 13–20. Entry free Mon–Thu in term time; Fri–Sun under 18: 3 €, adults 4 €. Check the site before going.<br><a href="https://i-punktskateland.de">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.0232,53.55144,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Skatepark Wilhelmsburg (Inselpark)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Former IGS garden-show grounds: ~1,700 m² of smooth concrete, ramps, rails, ledges, and a ~2 m deep bowl (the highlight).<br><br><b>Note:</b> Further south; S-Bahn to Wilhelmsburg. Best &#x27;proper&#x27; park for a skateboard-focused trip.<br><a href="https://www.inselpark.hamburg/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.00402,53.49344,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Skatepark Gleisbogen (Barmbek-Nord)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Opened 13 Sept 2024 under the elevated U-Bahn viaduct: quarter pipes, banks, London gap, pyramid with wallie ledge/rail, flat rail, plus a pumptrack.<br><br><b>Note:</b> OSM calls it &#x27;Am Gleisdreieck&#x27;; matched to hamburg.de&#x27;s park by location. Close to Cosmos Arcade and Retro Spiele Club.<br><a href="https://www.hamburg.de/freizeit/aktivitaeten/skateparks-hamburg-artikel-309220">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.0378,53.59099,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bunker Skatepark (Eimsbüttel)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Concrete skate area listed in OpenStreetMap as &#x27;Bunker Skatepark&#x27;.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Little info beyond OSM — treat as a bonus stop.]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95807,53.58124,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Skatepark Lenzsiedlung (Lokstedt)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Reopened summer 2023 after renovation: improved surface, modern elements, ~300 m², wheelchair-accessible.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Position geocoded from the street address (approx.).<br><i>Position approximate</i><br><a href="https://www.hamburg.de/freizeit/aktivitaeten/skateparks-hamburg-artikel-309220">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.94651,53.59001,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Skatepark Holstenstraße (St. Pauli)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Mini ramp with halfpipe, street section, pyramids, copings, bank, transition (per hamburg.de).<br><br><b>Note:</b> Position taken from the nearest concrete skate pitch in OSM — verify on arrival. Walkable from the Reeperbahn area.<br><i>Position approximate</i><br><a href="https://www.hamburg.de/freizeit/aktivitaeten/skateparks-hamburg-artikel-309220">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95234,53.55404,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Planten un Blomen skate area (Neustadt)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The ice rink becomes a 4,300 m² skate area, roughly April to end of Sept / mid-Oct.<br><br><b>Note:</b> ⚠ SEASONAL — likely closed now (it&#x27;s November). Pin is the park centre.<br><i>Position approximate</i><br><a href="https://www.hamburg.de/freizeit/aktivitaeten/skateparks-hamburg-artikel-309220">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.98133,53.56196,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Skatepark Rissen</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Forest setting: pipe, quarter, wallride, rail, curbs, banks, manual pad. Quiet.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Far west — only if you have a free afternoon.<br><a href="https://www.hamburg.de/freizeit/aktivitaeten/skateparks-hamburg-artikel-309220">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.77959,53.57931,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Allerfornia Skatepark (Neuallermöhe)</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Varied obstacles plus a 400 m² trend-sports area with slackline and calisthenics. Free, run by TSG Bergedorf.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Far east — low priority.<br><a href="https://www.hamburg.de/freizeit/aktivitaeten/skateparks-hamburg-artikel-309220">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.16918,53.48814,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Mantis Skateshop</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Skate shop in the city centre (OSM). Good for a stop if he needs bearings, grip or a new deck.<br><a href="https://mantisshop.de">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.99093,53.55628,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Lobby Skateshop</name><styleUrl>#skate</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Skate shop near Planten un Blomen (OSM).<br><a href="https://www.lobby-skateshop.de">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.97164,53.55829,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>⚓ History &amp; ferry</name><Placemark><name>Landungsbrücken – Pier 3 (ferry start)</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Boarding point for HVV harbour ferry Line 62 (Landungsbrücken → Altona Fischmarkt → Dockland → Neumühlen/Övelgönne → Bubendey-Ufer → Finkenwerder). It&#x27;s regular public transport, so it&#x27;s cheap and unscripted — a &#x27;mini harbour tour&#x27;.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Ride on a normal hvv ticket; timetable on hvv.de / hvv app / Google Maps. Weekend frequency in summer is higher than now — check the live timetable.<br><a href="https://hadag.de/en/routes/62/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.96931,53.5451,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>HADAG harbour tours</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[If you want commentary and a proper Hafenrundfahrt, HADAG runs dedicated harbour tours from the same piers.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Same area as Landungsbrücken; pin placed on Pier 3. Check seasonal schedule.<br><a href="https://hadag.de/en/harbour-tours/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.96931,53.5451,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fischmarkt Altona (ferry stop)</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Stop on Line 62. Historic fish-auction hall and bistro Liberté right at the pier with a view to the Elbphilharmonie. (The famous fish market itself runs Sunday mornings.)<br><a href="https://hadag.de/en/routes/62/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95284,53.54413,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Neumühlen / Övelgönne (ferry stop)</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Get off here for the Elbe beach promenade in Övelgönne with its museum harbour of old ships (Museumshafen). Great place to skip a stop and walk back.<br><a href="https://hadag.de/en/routes/62/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.91423,53.5435,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Museumshafen Övelgönne</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Open-air harbour of historic ships on the Elbe.]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.91446,53.54416,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Finkenwerder (end of Line 62)</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Terminus of the route — the Airbus works are across the water; a classic round trip back to Landungsbrücken.<br><a href="https://hadag.de/en/routes/62/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.8783,53.53684,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Alter Elbtunnel (St. Pauli Elbtunnel)</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Historic pedestrian/vehicle tunnel under the Elbe starting beside the Landungsbrücken — easy add-on to the ferry.]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.9666,53.54587,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rickmer Rickmers (museum ship)</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Historic three-masted museum ship moored at Landungsbrücken.<br><a href="https://www.rickmer-rickmers.de/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.97307,53.54456,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cap San Diego (museum ship)</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Large museum cargo ship at the Überseebrücke.<br><a href="https://www.capsandiego.de/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.97639,53.54314,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>St. Michaelis (Michel)</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Hamburg&#x27;s landmark baroque church.<br><a href="https://www.st-michaelis.de/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.97825,53.54887,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Speicherstadt</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Historic warehouse district (UNESCO World Heritage), good to walk through towards HafenCity.]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.987,53.544,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Internationales Maritimes Museum</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Maritime history museum in HafenCity.<br><a href="https://www.imm-hamburg.de/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.99997,53.54325,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Deutsches Hafenmuseum</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Museum of port history on the Kleiner Grasbrook.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Website didn&#x27;t respond during my check — verify the link/opening times.<br><a href="https://hafenmuseum-hamburg.de/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.9997,53.52541,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Miniatur Wunderland</name><styleUrl>#history</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[World&#x27;s largest model railway — a crowd-pleaser, especially with a gamer/tech-minded teen.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Book ahead; it&#x27;s often sold out on weekends.<br><a href="https://www.miniatur-wunderland.com/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.9894,53.54387,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>🎮 Games</name><Placemark><name>Retro Spiele Club (playable museum)</name><styleUrl>#games</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Playable museum of computers, consoles and software from the last 50 years. Visit during opening hours without registration. Moved from Horn (closed 2025) to Fuhlsbüttler Str. 490.<br><br><b>Note:</b> ⚠ HOURS: Mon/Thu/Fri 15–21, Sat 13–18; CLOSED Sunday. Under-18s must be accompanied (fine with you). Only Saturday works on a weekend trip. Verify on the site.<br><a href="https://www.retrospieleclub.de/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.03945,53.60798,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cosmos Arcade (Hamburger Meile)</name><styleUrl>#games</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[30+ arcade machines, racing simulators, air hockey and pinball (incl. Jurassic Park).<br><br><b>Note:</b> Hamburger Str. 39, Barmbek-Süd. Check opening times on the site.<br><a href="https://cosmosarcade.com/en/retro-arcade-hamburg">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>10.03205,53.57358,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>🎵 Music</name><Placemark><name>Beatles-Platz</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Tribute plaza at the Reeperbahn end of Große Freiheit with steel silhouettes of the five early Beatles.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Start of a short Beatles walk — everything below is within a few minutes on foot.<br><a href="https://www.hamburg-travel.com/see-explore/routes-tours/hamburg-and-the-beatles/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95733,53.54991,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Indra Club (Große Freiheit 64)</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Where the then-unknown Beatles played their first Hamburg gigs in 1960 after being invited by Bruno Koschmider.<br><a href="https://www.hamburg-travel.com/see-explore/routes-tours/hamburg-and-the-beatles/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95826,53.55209,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kaiserkeller (Große Freiheit 36)</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[One of the four Reeperbahn-area clubs the Beatles played 1960–62.<br><a href="https://www.hamburg-travel.com/see-explore/routes-tours/hamburg-and-the-beatles/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95808,53.55111,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Star-Club site (Große Freiheit 39)</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The Star-Club, the most famous of the Beatles&#x27; Hamburg venues.<br><a href="https://www.hamburg-travel.com/see-explore/routes-tours/hamburg-and-the-beatles/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95755,53.55108,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Top Ten Club site (Reeperbahn 136)</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[The Beatles&#x27; fourth Hamburg venue.<br><a href="https://www.hamburg-travel.com/see-explore/routes-tours/hamburg-and-the-beatles/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95954,53.54969,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Bambi Kino (Paul-Roosen-Straße)</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Cinema in a quiet side street where the Beatles were lodged in two windowless rooms next to the men&#x27;s toilet.<br><a href="https://mediaserver.hamburg.de/beatles-traces-in-st-pauli.html">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95758,53.55317,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Panik City (Udo Lindenberg)</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Multimedia museum experience about German rock star Udo Lindenberg and his Hamburg link (Hotel Atlantic, Reeperbahn).<br><br><b>Note:</b> Ticketed (~24.50 € listed on hamburg-travel for the morning tour). Check availability.<br><a href="https://www.die-roten-doppeldecker.de/en/panik-city-hamburg_en">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.96422,53.54902,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Molotow</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Well-known Reeperbahn-area indie club (now at Nobistor 14).<br><br><b>Note:</b> Evening venue — check programme.<br><a href="https://www.molotowclub.com">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95651,53.55012,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Gruenspan</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Historic live club on Große Freiheit.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Evening venue — check programme.<br><a href="https://www.gruenspan.de">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.95839,53.55181,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Elbphilharmonie (Plaza)</name><styleUrl>#music</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Concert hall on the harbour; the public Plaza viewing deck gives a great view over the port.<br><br><b>Note:</b> Plaza access normally needs a (free) timed ticket — check the site.<br><a href="https://www.elbphilharmonie.de/en/">Website</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>9.98538,53.54115,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder></Document></kml>